00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.950
It says here you can eat dandelions!

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:36.750
What are you reading?

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.250
A book about edible wild plants!

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.750
I borrowed it from the library!

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.120
Everyone knows about dandelions.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.830
Oh, yeah! 'Cause they put them on sashimi.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.500
People can eat that?

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.370
Those aren't dandelions, they're chrysanthemums.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.200
How do you know all that, Kotoha?

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.540
I learned things so that I could survive

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.540
after the rest of mankind is destroyed.

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:00.080
Three things.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.750
Wow! I think I would die!

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.000
Koto-chan is right!

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:10.950
If this town looks like it's gonna be wiped out,

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:10.950
WE have to survive, Leader!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:17.160
Which means that, to protect our town,

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:17.160
we have to find weeds that we can eat!

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.660
I bet there are a bunch in the park.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:24.620
Okay! Our mission is to figure out

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:24.620
which plants in the park we can eat!

